#
# Counter-example for math:ExtendedRealValueConstraint (the logic: gate on a
# signed-extended-real slot): a slot whose value is a NON-LITERAL IRI that is neither pole.
# The object of math:extendedRealValue is neither a literal nor one of the two poles
# math:PositiveInfinity / math:NegativeInfinity, so the projected sh:SPARQLConstraint bites
# and validation MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent (and no other finding). An IRI
# that is not a pole is not a point of ℝ̄ (math:MalformedExtendedReal).
# Bound by tests/example-conformance.ttl (ex:ecExtendedRealMalformed).
@prefix math: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/math/> .
@prefix ex:   <http://example.org/math/> .

ex:brokenReach math:extendedRealValue ex:notAPole .
